<title>ITALY: Italy's Palermo sees Sept CPI at 2.5 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Palermo sees Sept CPI at 2.5 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>PALERMO 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Palermo said its September consumer price index stood at 0.1 percent month-on-month and 2.5 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In August, Palermo's inflation rate was 0.1 percent and 2.5 percent respectively.  </p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 6.80 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.</p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to August 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.1   (0.1)     2.5  (2.5)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.2   (0.1)     4.2  (4.8)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.0   (0.0)     3.4  (3.4)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.2   (0.5)    -0.2 (-0.2)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0   (0.3)     2.6  (2.3)</p>
<p>    Health services		  -0.3   (0.0)     1.7  (2.2)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.0   (0.1)     3.2  (3.3)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.1   (0.1)     0.2  (0.1)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (0.0)     0.5  (5.6)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0   (0.0)     2.1  (2.2)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.1   (0.0)     0.3  (0.0)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom ++392 66129526</p>
